WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:11.280
21. Hanging on the go. Don't get too attached to your wallet. One day it will belong in

2
00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:16.800
a museum, along with everything in it. That's because credit cards and cash are being replaced

3
00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:23.060
by mobile payments made on smartphones. Mobile payments are changing the way we shop, and

4
00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:29.840
they're doing it quickly. There are now over 4.8 billion smartphone owners in the world.

5
00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:36.660
In the United States, 39% of smartphone users made at least one mobile payment in 2015.

6
00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:43.640
That's up from just 14% in 2014. But what are mobile payments? Well, there are a few

7
00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:49.100
different types. First, they are everyday payments you can make on your smartphone.

8
00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:53.840
This would include opening up an internet browser and buying a new pair of shoes. There

9
00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:58.360
are also point-of-sale payments and mobile wallet apps. These are for when you're at

10
00:00:58.360 --> 00:01:03.340
Starbucks or McDonald's and want to pay with your smartphone. Various other apps can

11
00:01:03.340 --> 00:01:08.500
help you manage your money with your smartphone. Banking apps, for example, let you easily

12
00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:14.180
send money to friends and relatives and are very popular. Mobile payments are a potential

13
00:01:14.180 --> 00:01:19.860
game changer. For example, just imagine if every store in the world used the same point-of-sale

14
00:01:19.860 --> 00:01:25.580
system. You could safely use your smartphone to buy things from anywhere on the planet.

15
00:01:25.580 --> 00:01:30.680
Vacation shopping would never be the same. But let's not forget the one biggest advantage

16
00:01:30.680 --> 00:01:35.800
of this brave new world of mobile payments. It would make losing your phone even more

17
00:01:35.800 --> 00:01:36.840
of a nightmare.
